# exempt: record()'s remaining begin_account_scoped call (user_id: None branch, inside the Some(account_id) arm) is PERMANENT, not unfinished -- it is the consumer-JobScope path (JobScope::usage_account_id returns None on the Org arm by design), and is unrelated to the user_id-threaded begin_tenant_scoped branch added for request-path callers. reserve(), finalize() and record() each carry the SAME three-way branch, and the account_id: None arm of all three opens begin_tenant_system_scoped_without_account (usage.rs:495, :631, :1750) -- a real transaction-local app.tenant_actor='system', not an ambient insert. Exempt rather than converted because the consumer arm's literal begin_account_scoped( call stays, and the script's converted bar is zero such calls, which a two-plane branch can never meet. CORRECTED (this PR): the previous rationale justified the four tenant-loop worker callers passing user_id: None with "their pool is already the Category C system-scoped worker pool". No such pool exists. PR #388 (21980710) deleted the -c app.tenant_actor=system connection STARTUP option because a pooler rejects unknown startup parameters, and tenancy/registry.rs::connect_and_verify now builds the worker pool with a plain PgPoolOptions::connect that sets no session GUC at all. What makes those callers correct is the Rust-level None arm above, nothing about the pool. This file is the one entry here reached from BOTH the worker pool and the REQUEST pool, so both OPS-4-T failure modes apply: on the worker pool tenancy::registry::worker_pool_rls_exemption_breach runs on every build and refuses a NOBYPASSRLS role outright (WorkerPoolNotRlsExempt -- the tenant's background work stops with a logged error, it does not read empty); on the request pool there is NO tripwire (connect_and_verify asserts only when is_worker_pool), so an unscoped insert would raise 42501 and record() would downgrade it to a warn! under its best-effort contract -- a silently missing metering row. That second mode is exactly why the None arm was converted instead of left resting on the owner exemption.
