# exempt: tenant-loop worker (workers::tenant_harness). All 30 literal begin_account_scoped( calls in this file are JobScope::Consumer arms -- app.account_id, the pre-existing OPS-4 consumer-plane mechanism, permanent -- which is why this file is exempt and not converted (the converted bar is zero such calls, which a two-plane branch can never meet). CORRECTED (this PR): the previous rationale credited the Org arm to "tenancy::registry::TenantRegistry::get_or_build_worker_pool's connection-scoped app.tenant_actor=system". PR #388 (21980710) deleted that STARTUP-packet option because a connection pooler rejects unknown startup parameters; connect_and_verify now builds the worker pool with a plain PgPoolOptions::connect and sets no session GUC. TEN real scope defects fixed here -- every JobScope::Org arm in this file that issued its own query instead of going through Store. scoped_self_node_id (graphs), scoped_provisional_node_ids (nodes), scoped_provisional_seed_rows (nodes), clear_provisional_flag (UPDATE nodes), scoped_pair_has_active_unsure (reef_judgement), trgm_candidate_pairs (nodes self-join, one scope per keyset page, mirroring its consumer arm), load_nodes_by_ids (nodes LEFT JOIN node_atoms), and the three §10.5 identity-door gauges scoped_rebirths_24h (nodes, reef_identifiers), scoped_twins_24h (node_merges) and scoped_stale_provisional (nodes, reef_judgement) -- the last three via a bare pool.acquire(). Each ran ambient while the SAME function's Consumer arm opened a transaction. Every table listed carries a member_ocean_isolation policy resolving through tenant_rls_visible_graph_ids(), which hides every member-ocean and team graph unless the transaction has set app.tenant_actor or app.user_id (org and personal graphs stay visible: tenant_rls_actor_user_id() is NULL when unset, so both conjuncts of the non-system branch are trivially true for them); both are set_config(..,true), so a statement against a pooled &PgPool cannot carry either. (reef_identifiers' policy is migrations_tenant/0045, reef_judgement's is 0046 -- not 0009.) All ten now open begin_tenant_system_scoped_without_account, same shape as workers::roster::build_scoped. SLICE 4 (this PR) cleared the twenty store-mediated Org arms: each called the unscoped Store method where the Consumer arm called its _scoped twin, and each now opens begin_tenant_system_scoped_without_account and calls that twin. Fourteen are reads and six are writes (set_er_sweep_cursor, merge_nodes, insert_merge_dismissal, write_judgement, annul_judgement, merge_nodes_with_judgement); all twenty commit, mirroring their own Consumer arms. scoped_atom_inline_content needed care: its Consumer arm inlines the SQL rather than calling the trait, and the doc claiming no _scoped twin exists was stale -- atom_inline_content_scoped runs the identical SQL, so the Org arm calls it. scoped_get_node_entity_type_hint discards its error with .ok(), so a scope that never opened would have read as "no hint"; it now logs that case at warn. resolve_graph's JobScope match pulls out a &PgPool only to hand to llm::usage, which scopes its own writes (see its entry above) -- not a gap. No JobScope::Org arm in this file runs a statement on the bare pool now. The owner exemption (0009 §7 does not FORCE row security), asserted at pool build by tenancy::registry::worker_pool_rls_exemption_breach, is a second line rather than the only cover; at OPS-4-T the pool refuses to build and entity resolution stops with a logged error for that tenant, rather than merging over an empty candidate set.
